   Game Title: Light Platformer
   Core Concept: A 2D platformer where light reveals safe platforms, and darkness hides hazards (spikes). Platforms only appear when a light source is within range; spikes only appear in darkness. Player must navigate using light to reveal safe paths, avoid hazards in darkness, and reach the exit.
   Core Mechanics:
   - Player Movement: 2D platformer physics, gravity, jump, run.
   - Light Source: Dynamic light source (mouse or AI) with limited radius.
   - Platform Generation: Platforms appear only when within light radius; vanish when outside radius.
   - Hazard Generation: Spikes appear only when darkness exceeds light radius or light is absent.
   - Collision Detection: AABB or pixel-perfect between player and hazards/platforms.
   - Light Radius Visualization: Dynamic light radius rendered on canvas, possibly with glow/gradient.
   UI/HUD: Light radius indicator, Darkness toggle, Score, Lives, Start menu.
   Win Condition: Light radius covers all safe platforms and no spikes within radius, OR player reaches exit platform.
